  "content": {
    "rendered": "\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"727\" src=\"https://quranbook.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/99-names-of-Allah-PDF-1024x727.png\" alt=\"99 names of Allah PDF\" class=\"wp-image-6059\" srcset=\"https://quranbook.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/99-names-of-Allah-PDF-1024x727.png 1024w, https://quranbook.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/99-names-of-Allah-PDF-300x213.png 300w, https://quranbook.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/99-names-of-Allah-PDF-768x545.png 768w, https://quranbook.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/99-names-of-Allah-PDF.png 1124w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">99 names of Allah PDF</p>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:100px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><a href=\"https://understandquran.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/99Names-2019.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"256\" height=\"256\" src=\"https://quranbook.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/PDF1.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5730\" style=\"width:148px;height:auto\" srcset=\"https://quranbook.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/PDF1.png 256w, https://quranbook.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/PDF1-150x150.png 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 256px) 100vw, 256px\" /></a></figure>\n</div>\n\n\n<div style=\"height:100px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Arabic Name</th><th>Transliteration</th><th>English Translation</th><th>Arabic Explanation</th><th>English Explanation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>الله</td><td>Allah</td><td>Allah</td><td>هو الاسم الدال على الذات الجامعة لصفات الألوهية.</td><td>The name indicating the essence that encompasses all divine attributes.</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>الرّحمن</td><td>Ar-Rahman</td><td>The Beneficent</td><td>واسع الرحمة في خلقه مؤمنهم وكافرهم.</td><td>The one whose mercy extends over all creation, believers and disbelievers alike.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>الرّحيم</td><td>Ar-Rahim</td><td>The Merciful</td><td>المعطي من الثواب أضعاف العمل.</td><td>The one who gives reward greater than the action itself.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>الملك</td><td>Al-Malik</td><td>The King</td><td>المتصرّف في ملكه كما يشاء.</td><td>The one who rules over His dominion as He wills.</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>القدوس</td><td>Al-Quddus</td><td>The Most Sacred</td><td>المنزه عن كل وصف يدركه حسٌ أو خيال.</td><td>The one free from any attribute perceptible by the senses or imagination.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>السلام</td><td>As-Salam</td><td>The Source of Peace</td><td>السالم من العيوب والنقائص والناشر سلامته على خلقه.</td><td>The one free from defects and imperfections and the giver of peace to His creation.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>المؤمن</td><td>Al-Mu’min</td><td>The Guarantor</td><td>المصدق نفسه وكتبه ورسله فيما يقولونه عنه.</td><td>The one who assures the truth of His own being, His books, and His messengers.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>المهيمن</td><td>Al-Muhaymin</td><td>The Guardian</td><td>المسيطر على كل شيء بكماله وقوته.</td><td>The one who watches over and controls all things with His perfect power.</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>العزيز</td><td>Al-Aziz</td><td>The Almighty</td><td>الغالب الذي لا نظير له.</td><td>The one who is unrivaled and overpowering.</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>الجبار</td><td>Al-Jabbar</td><td>The Compeller</td><td>المنفذ مشيئته على سبيل الإجبار والجبر.</td><td>The one who enforces His will without opposition.</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>المتكبّر</td><td>Al-Mutakabbir</td><td>The Supreme</td><td>المتفرد بصفات العظمة والكبرياء.</td><td>The one who is uniquely supreme in His greatness and majesty.</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>الخالق</td><td>Al-Khaliq</td><td>The Creator</td><td>المبدع لخلقه بإرادته.</td><td>The one who creates everything with His will.</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>البارئ</td><td>Al-Bari</td><td>The Evolver</td><td>المميِّز لخلقه بالصور المختلفة.</td><td>The one who shapes His creation in different forms.</td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>المصوّر</td><td>Al-Musawwir</td><td>The Fashioner</td><td>الذي أعطى لكل خلق صورة خاصة.</td><td>The one who gives each of His creations a distinct appearance.</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>الغفّار</td><td>Al-Ghaffar</td><td>The Great Forgiver</td><td>الذي يستر القبيح في الدنيا ويتجاوز عنه في الآخرة.</td><td>The one who covers up sins in the world and forgives them in the Hereafter.</td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>القهّار</td><td>Al-Qahhar</td><td>The All-Prevailing</td><td>الذي يقهر الجبابرة.</td><td>The one who subdues the tyrants.</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>الوهّاب</td><td>Al-Wahhab</td><td>The Supreme Bestower</td><td>المتفضّل بالعطايا.</td><td>The one who grants gifts generously.</td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>الرّزاق</td><td>Ar-Razzaq</td><td>The Provider</td><td>خالق الأرزاق والمتكفّل بإيصالها إلى خلقه.</td><td>The one who creates and provides sustenance to His creation.</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>الفتاح</td><td>Al-Fattah</td><td>The Opener</td><td>الذي يفتح خزائن رحمته لعباده.</td><td>The one who opens the treasures of His mercy to His servants.</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>العليم</td><td>Al-‘Alim</td><td>The All-Knowing</td><td>المحيط علمه بكل شيء.</td><td>The one whose knowledge encompasses everything.</td></tr><tr><td>21</td><td>القابض</td><td>Al-Qabid</td><td>The Withholder</td><td>قابض يده عمن يشاء.</td><td>The one who withholds His bounty from whom He wills.</td></tr><tr><td>22</td><td>الباسط</td><td>Al-Basit</td><td>The Extender</td><td>بأسراره ورزقه على من يشاء.</td><td>The one who extends His bounty and secrets to whom He wills.</td></tr><tr><td>23</td><td>الخافض</td><td>Al-Khafid</td><td>The Reducer</td><td>الذي يخفض الكفار والأشقياء المتكبرين.</td><td>The one who brings down the disbelievers and arrogant.</td></tr><tr><td>24</td><td>الرّافع</td><td>Ar-Rafi’</td><td>The Exalter</td><td>للأقدار بين أولياء الرجال، فهو يرفع عباده الطائعين بعبادتهم.</td><td>The one who elevates the ranks of righteous believers through their worship.</td></tr><tr><td>25</td><td>المعزّ</td><td>Al-Mu’izz</td><td>The Honourer-Bestower</td><td>للمؤمنين بطاعته فيعطيهم القوة والغلبة والشدة لمن شاء.</td><td>The one who grants honor, strength, and glory to the believers by His obedience.</td></tr><tr><td>26</td><td>المذل</td><td>Al-Mudhill</td><td>The Dishonourer</td><td>للكافرين بعصيانهم.</td><td>The one who humiliates the disbelievers due to their disobedience.</td></tr><tr><td>27</td><td>السّميع</td><td>As-Sami’</td><td>The All-Hearing</td><td>الذي لا يغيب عنه مسموع، ويحيط بجميع الأصوات الظاهرة والباطنة والخفية والجلية.</td><td>The one who is not unaware of any sound, encompassing all audible and inaudible, hidden and evident sounds.</td></tr><tr><td>28</td><td>البصير</td><td>Al-Basir</td><td>The All-Seeing</td><td>الذي يشاهد جميع الموجودات ويرى الأشياء كلها ظاهرها وباطنها.</td><td>The one who observes all things and sees all visible and hidden matters.</td></tr><tr><td>29</td><td>الحكم</td><td>Al-Hakam</td><td>The Judge</td><td>الذي إليه ترجع الأمور والأحكام فيفصل بين الحق والباطل ولا راد لقضائه.</td><td>The one to whom all affairs return, and He decides between right and wrong with no one to overturn His judgment.</td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>العدل</td><td>Al-Adl</td><td>The Utterly Just</td><td>الذي ليس في ملكه خلل وهو الذي حرم الظلم على نفسه.</td><td>The one in whose dominion there is no flaw, and who has forbidden oppression on Himself.</td></tr><tr><td>31</td><td>اللّطيف</td><td>Al-Latif</td><td>The Subtle One</td><td>البرّ الرفيق بعباده يرزق ويحسن إليهم.</td><td>The kind and gentle one who provides sustenance and does good to His servants.</td></tr><tr><td>32</td><td>الخبير</td><td>Al-Khabir</td><td>The Acquainted</td><td>العالم بكل شيء باطن أو ظاهر.</td><td>The one who knows everything, apparent and hidden.</td></tr><tr><td>33</td><td>الحليم</td><td>Al-Halim</td><td>The Forbearing</td><td>الذي لا يعجل بالعقاب فهو يمهل ولا يهمل.</td><td>The one who does not hasten to punish, but rather gives time and does not neglect.</td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>العظيم</td><td>Al-Azim</td><td>The Magnificent</td><td>الذي لا تصل العقول إلى كُنه ذاته.</td><td>The one whose essence is beyond the reach of intellects.</td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>الغفور</td><td>Al-Ghafur</td><td>The Forgiving</td><td>غافر الذنب وقابل التوب.</td><td>The one who forgives sins and accepts repentance.</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>الشّكور</td><td>Ash-Shakur</td><td>The Most Appreciative</td><td>المنعم على عباده بالثواب، ويتقبّل أعمال عباده ويُضاعف أجرها.</td><td>The one who grants rewards to His servants, accepts their deeds, and multiplies their rewards.</td></tr><tr><td>37</td><td>العليّ</td><td>Al-Ali</td><td>The Most High</td><td>الذي علا بذاته وصفاته عن مدارج الخلق.</td><td>The one who is exalted in His essence and attributes above all creation.</td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>الكبير</td><td>Al-Kabir</td><td>The Most Great</td><td>المُنزه عن الأوهام فهو العظيم الذي ليس كمثله شيء.</td><td>The one who is free from illusions, the great who is incomparable.</td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td>الحفيظ</td><td>Al-Hafiz</td><td>The Preserver</td><td>حافظ الكون من الخلل.</td><td>The one who preserves the universe from disruption.</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>المقيت</td><td>Al-Muqit</td><td>The Sustainer</td><td>خالق الأقوات ومُقسمها والمتكفّل بإيصالها للمخلوقات.</td><td>The one who creates, distributes, and ensures the sustenance of His creation.</td></tr><tr><td>41</td><td>الحسيب</td><td>Al-Hasib</td><td>The Reckoner</td><td>الذي يكفي عباده حاجتهم.</td><td>The one who suffices His servants’ needs.</td></tr><tr><td>42</td><td>الجليل</td><td>Al-Jalil</td><td>The Majestic</td><td>عظيم القدر بجلاله وكماله.</td><td>The one of great honor and perfect majesty.</td></tr><tr><td>43</td><td>الكريم</td><td>Al-Karim</td><td>The Most Generous</td><td>الذي لا ينفذ عطاؤه.</td><td>The one whose generosity never ceases.</td></tr><tr><td>44</td><td>الرّقيب</td><td>Ar-Raqib</td><td>The Watchful</td><td>الملاحظ لما يرعاهم فهو المراقب لأحوال العباد ويعلم أقوالهم وأفعالهم.</td><td>The one who observes and watches over His creation, aware of their words and deeds.</td></tr><tr><td>45</td><td>المُجيب</td><td>Al-Mujib</td><td>The Responsive One</td><td>الذي يجيب الداعي إذا دعاه والسائل إذا سأله.</td><td>The one who responds to the caller when they call upon Him and answers the one who asks.</td></tr><tr><td>46</td><td>الواسع</td><td>Al-Wasi’</td><td>The All-Encompassing</td><td>الذي وسع رزقه جميع خلقه.</td><td>The one whose sustenance encompasses all of His creation.</td></tr><tr><td>47</td><td>الحكيم</td><td>Al-Hakim</td><td>The All-Wise</td><td>المُنزه عن فعل ما لا ينبغي بجلاله وكماله، المحقق في تدبيره، اللطيف في تقديره.</td><td>The one who is free from doing what is unbecoming of His majesty and perfection, precise in His planning, and gentle in His estimation.</td></tr><tr><td>48</td><td>الودود</td><td>Al-Wadud</td><td>The Most Loving</td><td>المتحبب إلى خلقه محب لهم والمحبوب في قلوب أوليائه.</td><td>The one who loves His creation and is loved by the hearts of His devotees.</td></tr><tr><td>49</td><td>المجيد</td><td>Al-Majid</td><td>The Glorious</td><td>الشريف في ذاته وأفعاله، والجزيل في عطائه.</td><td>The one who is noble in His essence and actions, generous in His giving.</td></tr><tr><td>50</td><td>الباعث</td><td>Al-Ba’ith</td><td>The Resurrector</td><td>باعث الموتى للحساب.</td><td>The one who raises the dead for accountability.</td></tr><tr><td>51</td><td>الشهيد</td><td>Ash-Shahid</td><td>The Witness</td><td>الحاضر الذي لا يغيب عنه شيء فهو العالم بالأمور ظاهرها وباطنها.</td><td>The one who is ever-present and aware of all things, apparent and hidden.</td></tr><tr><td>52</td><td>الحق</td><td>Al-Haqq</td><td>The Truth</td><td>خالق كل شيء بحكمة.</td><td>The one who creates everything with wisdom.</td></tr><tr><td>53</td><td>الوكيل</td><td>Al-Wakil</td><td>The Trustee</td><td>الكفيل بالخلق القائم بأمورهم فهو الموكول إليه الأمور كلها.</td><td>The one who is entrusted with the affairs of His creation, managing all matters.</td></tr><tr><td>54</td><td>القويّ</td><td>Al-Qawiyy</td><td>The Most Strong</td><td>الذي لا يعجزه شيء وصاحب القدرة التامة البالغة الكمال.</td><td>The one who is not incapacitated by anything and possesses complete and perfect power.</td></tr><tr><td>55</td><td>المتين</td><td>Al-Matin</td><td>The Firm One</td><td>الذي لا يُغلب ولا يحتاج إلى مدد وعون في إمضاء حكمه.</td><td>The one who is undefeatable and needs no assistance in enforcing His decrees.</td></tr><tr><td>56</td><td>الوليّ</td><td>Al-Wali</td><td>The Protecting Associate</td><td>المحب لأوليائه الناصر لهم.</td><td>The one who loves and supports His allies.</td></tr><tr><td>57</td><td>الحميد</td><td>Al-Hamid</td><td>The Praiseworthy</td><td>المستحق للحمد والثناء.</td><td>The one who is deserving of praise and gratitude.</td></tr><tr><td>58</td><td>المحصي</td><td>Al-Muhsi</td><td>The All-Enumerating One</td><td>الذي أحصى كل شيء بعلمه، الذي أحاط كل مخلوقاته بعلمه.</td><td>The one who has counted everything in knowledge and encompasses all His creations in knowledge.</td></tr><tr><td>59</td><td>المُبدئ</td><td>Al-Mubdi</td><td>The Originator</td><td>الذي بدأ الخلق وأوجده من العدم.</td><td>The one who initiates creation and brings it into existence from nothing.</td></tr><tr><td>60</td><td>المعيد</td><td>Al-Mu’id</td><td>The Restorer</td><td>الذي يعيد الخلق إلى الموت.</td><td>The one who returns creation to death.</td></tr><tr><td>61</td><td>المحيي</td><td>Al-Muhyi</td><td>The Giver of Life</td><td>الذي يحيي العظام وهي رميم.</td><td>The one who gives life to bones while they are decayed.</td></tr><tr><td>62</td><td>المميت</td><td>Al-Mumit</td><td>The Creator of Death</td><td>الذي يميت الأجسام بنزع الأرواح منها.</td><td>The one who causes bodies to die by removing their souls.</td></tr><tr><td>63</td><td>الحيّ</td><td>Al-Hayy</td><td>The Ever-Living</td><td>المتصف بالحياة الأبدية.</td><td>The one characterized by eternal life.</td></tr><tr><td>64</td><td>القيوم</td><td>Al-Qayyum</td><td>The Sustainer</td><td>القائم بنفسه الغني عن غيره.</td><td>The one who is self-sustaining, independent of others.</td></tr><tr><td>65</td><td>الواجد</td><td>Al-Wajid</td><td>The Perceiver</td><td>الذي يجد كل ما يطلبه ويريده.</td><td>The one who finds all that He seeks and desires.</td></tr><tr><td>66</td><td>الماجد</td><td>Al-Majid</td><td>The Illustrious</td><td>كبير الإحسان والأفضال.</td><td>The one of great beneficence and generosity.</td></tr><tr><td>67</td><td>الواحد</td><td>Al-Wahid</td><td>The One</td><td>المتفرد ذاتًا ووصفًا وأفعالًا.</td><td>The one who is unique in essence, attributes, and actions.</td></tr><tr><td>68</td><td>الصّمد</td><td>As-Samad</td><td>The Eternal</td><td>المقصود بالحوائج، فهو المطاع الذي لا يقضى دونه أمر.</td><td>The one who is sought for needs, the one obeyed without having anything decreed without His permission.</td></tr><tr><td>69</td><td>القادر</td><td>Al-Qadir</td><td>The Omnipotent</td><td>المتفرد باختراع الموجودات.</td><td>The one who is unique in creating existence.</td></tr><tr><td>70</td><td>المقتدر</td><td>Al-Muqtadir</td><td>The Creator of All Power</td><td>الذي يقدر على ما يشاء.</td><td>The one who has power over everything.</td></tr><tr><td>71</td><td>المؤخر</td><td>Al-Mu’akhkhir</td><td>The Delayer</td><td>مؤخر الأعداء بالإبعاد.</td><td>The one who delays the enemies by distancing them.</td></tr><tr><td>72</td><td>الأول</td><td>Al-Awwal</td><td>The First</td><td>السابق للأشياء.</td><td>The one who precedes everything.</td></tr><tr><td>73</td><td>الآخر</td><td>Al-Akhir</td><td>The Last</td><td>الباقي بعد فناء خلقه.</td><td>The one who remains after the annihilation of creation.</td></tr><tr><td>74</td><td>الظّاهر</td><td>Az-Zahir</td><td>The Manifest</td><td>بآياته وعلامات قدرته.</td><td>The one whose signs and power are evident.</td></tr><tr><td>75</td><td>الباطن</td><td>Al-Batin</td><td>The Hidden</td><td>المحتجب عن الأنظار والمطلع على الأسرار.</td><td>The one concealed from sight but aware of all secrets.</td></tr><tr><td>76</td><td>الوالي</td><td>Al-Wali</td><td>The Sole Governor</td><td>المالك للأشياء والمتصرف فيها كيف يشاء.</td><td>The one who owns things and manages them as He wills.</td></tr><tr><td>77</td><td>المتعالي</td><td>Al-Muta’ali</td><td>The Self-Exalted</td><td>رفيع الدرجات ذو العرش المرتفع في كبريائه وعظمته.</td><td>The one exalted in ranks, the possessor of the elevated throne, great in His majesty and grandeur.</td></tr><tr><td>78</td><td>البر</td><td>Al-Barr</td><td>The Source of All Goodness</td><td>الذي يمنُّ على السائلين بحسن العطاء.</td><td>The one who bestows His kindness upon those who ask.</td></tr><tr><td>79</td><td>التّواب</td><td>At-Tawwab</td><td>The Ever-Pardoning</td><td>يقبل التوبة عن عباده ويعفو عن سيئاتهم.</td><td>The one who accepts the repentance of His servants and forgives their sins.</td></tr><tr><td>80</td><td>المنتقم</td><td>Al-Muntaqim</td><td>The Avenger</td><td>الذي نخشى نقمته لقدرته وعظمته.</td><td>The one whose vengeance is feared due to His power and greatness.</td></tr><tr><td>81</td><td>العفوّ</td><td>Al-‘Afuww</td><td>The Pardoner</td><td>الذي يمحو الذنوب ويتجاوز عن السيئات.</td><td>The one who erases sins and overlooks faults.</td></tr><tr><td>82</td><td>الرّؤوف</td><td>Ar-Ra’uf</td><td>The Most Kind</td><td>شديد الرحمة بعباده.</td><td>The one of extreme mercy towards His servants.</td></tr><tr><td>83</td><td>مالك المُلك</td><td>Malik-ul-Mulk</td><td>Master of the Kingdom</td><td>له التصرف المطلق وهو تعالى الذي ينفذ مشيئته في ملكه كيف يشاء وكما يشاء.</td><td>The one with absolute authority who executes His will in His dominion as He wishes.</td></tr><tr><td>84</td><td>ذو الجلال والإكرام</td><td>Dhul-Jalali Wal-Ikram</td><td>Lord of Glory and Honour</td><td>المنفرد بصفات الجلال والكمال والعظمة المختص بالإكرام والكرامة.</td><td>The one unique in attributes of majesty, perfection, and greatness, exclusive in honor and dignity.</td></tr><tr><td>85</td><td>المُقسط</td><td>Al-Muqsiṭ</td><td>The Just One</td><td>القائم بالقسط والمقيم بالعدل.</td><td>The one who upholds equity and justice.</td></tr><tr><td>86</td><td>الجامع</td><td>Al-Jami’</td><td>The Gatherer</td><td>الذي جمع الكمالات كلها ذاتًا ووصفًا وفعلًا.</td><td>The one who has gathered all perfections in essence, attributes, and actions.</td></tr><tr><td>87</td><td>الغني</td><td>Al-Ghani</td><td>The Self-Sufficient</td><td>الذي لا يحتاج إلى شيء.</td><td>The one who is in no need of anything.</td></tr><tr><td>88</td><td>المغني</td><td>Al-Mughni</td><td>The Enricher</td><td>المعطي لمن يشاء من عباده.</td><td>The one who enriches whom He wills from His servants.</td></tr><tr><td>89</td><td>المانع</td><td>Al-Mani’</td><td>The Withholder</td><td>الذي يمنع البلاء حفظًا وعناية، ويمنع العطاء عمن يشاء ابتلاء وحماية.</td><td>The one who withholds harm as protection and withholds giving from whom He wills as a trial and protection.</td></tr><tr><td>90</td><td>الضّار</td><td>Ad-Darr</td><td>The Creator of The Harmful</td><td>هو المقدر للضر لمن يشاء.</td><td>The one who decrees harm for whom He wills.</td></tr><tr><td>91</td><td>النّافع</td><td>An-Nafi’</td><td>The Creator of Good</td><td>المقدر للنفع ومالكه.</td><td>The one who decrees and possesses benefit.</td></tr><tr><td>92</td><td>النّور</td><td>An-Nur</td><td>The Light</td><td>الهادي الرشيد الذي أرشد ونور قلوب الصادقين بتوحيده.</td><td>The one who guides and enlightens the hearts of the truthful with His oneness.</td></tr><tr><td>93</td><td>الهادي</td><td>Al-Hadi</td><td>The Guide</td><td>الذي أعطى كل شيء خلقه ثم هدى، المبين لطريق الحق.</td><td>The one who gave everything its form and then guided it, showing the path of truth.</td></tr><tr><td>94</td><td>البديع</td><td>Al-Badi’</td><td>The Incomparable</td><td>الذي لا يماثله أحد في صفاته ولا في أفعاله ولا في أحكامه أو أي أمر من أموره.</td><td>The one who is unparalleled in His attributes, actions, judgments, or any of His matters.</td></tr><tr><td>95</td><td>الباقي</td><td>Al-Baqi</td><td>The Everlasting</td><td>الدائم الوجود الموصوف بالبقاء.</td><td>The one of everlasting existence, characterized by permanence.</td></tr><tr><td>96</td><td>الوارث</td><td>Al-Warith</td><td>The Inheritor of All</td><td>من له ما في السماوات والأرض، رب كل شيء ووارثه ورازقه وراحمه.</td><td>The one to whom belongs everything in the heavens and the earth, the Lord, inheritor, provider, and merciful of all things.</td></tr><tr><td>97</td><td>الرّشيد</td><td>Ar-Rashid</td><td>The Righteous Teacher</td><td>المرشد لأهل الطاعة، فأرشد من شاء بإرشاده وأشقى من شاء بإبعاده.</td><td>The one who guides the obedient, guiding whom He wills and distancing whom He wills.</td></tr><tr><td>98</td><td>الصّبور</td><td>As-Sabur</td><td>The Patient</td><td>الذي يمهل وينظر ولا يعجل ولا يعاجل ولا يسارع وينزل الأمر بقدر معلوم.</td><td>The one who grants respite, watches, does not hasten, does not rush, and decrees matters with precise measure.</td></tr><tr><td>99</td><td>المبين</td><td>Al-Mubin</td><td>The Clear One</td><td></td><td>The one who is clear and manifests the truth.</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">99 names of Allah PDF</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This table includes the Arabic name, its transliteration, the English translation, the Arabic explanation, and its English translation for each of the 99 names of Allah.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\"><a href=\"https://quranbook.org/%d8%a7%d8%b3%d9%85%d8%a7%d8%a1-%d8%a7%d9%84%d9%84%d9%87-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ad%d8%b3%d9%86%d9%89-%d8%b9%d9%86%d8%af-%d8%a7%d9%87%d9%84-%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%b3%d9%86%d9%87-%d9%88%d8%a7%d9%84%d8%ac%d9%85%d8%a7/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">اسماء الله الحسنى</a></h2>\n",
